openrouter_oauth_button base vs new comparison:

Base `_startFlow`:
```
String? code;
if (onCapture != null) { code = await onCapture!(authUrl); }
if (code == null || code.isEmpty) {
 final launched = await launchUrl(authUrl, ...);
 if (!launched) return;
 if (context.mounted) { code = await _showCodeSheet(context); }
if (code == null || code.isEmpty) return;
if (!context.mounted) return;
final strings = ...;
try { key = await exchange...; if (context.mounted) onSuccess...}
on ConfigException -> snack if mounted
on Object -> snack if mounted
```

New `_startFlow`:
```
final code = await _acquireCode(context, authUrl);
if (code == null || code.isEmpty) return;
if (!context.mounted) return;
await _exchangeKey(context, code, verifier);
```

`_acquireCode`:
```
Future<String?> pasteFallback() => _pastedCodeAfterLaunch(context, authUrl);
return _capturedCode(authUrl).then((captured) => (captured == null || captured.isEmpty) ? pasteFallback() : captured);
```

Check semantic equivalence:
- Base: if onCapture != null → await capture. New `_capturedCode` handles null → null. Equivalent.
- Base: if code null/empty → launchUrl; if !launched → return (i.e., code stays null → return null overall). New `_pastedCodeAfterLaunch`: if !launched return null; then sheet. Equivalent.
- Base: `if (context.mounted) { code = await _showCodeSheet(context); }` — if context not mounted after launch, code stays null → returns null. New: `if (!context.mounted) return null; return _showCodeSheet(context);` Equivalent.
- Then `if (code == null || code.isEmpty) return;` same.
- `if (!context.mounted) return;` — base had this AFTER the code emptiness check, before strings/exchange. New: also after. ✓
- Exchange: base try/catch with mounted-guarded snack on ConfigException and Object. New `_exchangeKey` with showError closure → `_showOAuthError` checks mounted. Equivalent ✓.

One subtle: base declared `final strings = FaUiStrings.of(context);` after the mounted check; new `_exchangeKey` reads strings at top (before try) — strings read happens after the mounted check in `_startFlow`, so context valid. Fine.

Another subtle: base evaluated the exchange and errors with `strings` captured before the await — new `showError` closure captures `strings` similarly. ✓

Async boundary: base's sequential awaits vs new's `.then` composition — the `.then` on `_capturedCode(authUrl)`: `_capturedCode` is an async function, so `.then` fires in a later microtask — no behavioral change observable (no setState between).

One potential difference: in base, if onCapture throws, the exception propagates out of _startFlow unhandled — same in new (the .then would propagate the error through the returned future). ✓ Equivalent.

